From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: asus-rog5-ams678: send the full 10-bit DBV

With the msm command DMA FIFO fix (dma_fifo_ctrl) the whole DCS 0x51 packet
reaches the panel, so drop the three-level quantisation that mapped
1..1023 onto DBV 0x100/0x200/0x300 and send the backlight value as the
10-bit DBV, as stock does (bl_ctrl_dcs, 1..1023, inverted DBV). The packet
on the wire is unchanged in shape: DCS long write 0x51 with the two payload
bytes {DBV[15:8], DBV[7:0]} ("39 ... 03 51 hh ll"). Keep stock's DBV
substitutions 1 -> 2 and 9 -> 10 (dsi_anakin_backlightupdate). LP transfer
stays the default; bl_hs=1 selects stock's HS mode once verified.

Userspace: max_brightness stays 1023 and the levels are linear DBV, so
gsd-power/Phosh (percent -> level through logind SetBrightness) get 1023
steps without any change.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c
@@ -101,6 +101,15 @@
 static unsigned int te_scanline = 0x0980;
 module_param(te_scanline, uint, 0644);
 
+/*
+ * Brightness transfer mode. Stock sends the DBV in HS mode; the LP path is
+ * what worked before the DSI command DMA FIFO fix (msm dma_fifo_ctrl), so it
+ * stays the default until HS is verified on the phone.
+ */
+static bool bl_hs;
+module_param(bl_hs, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bl_hs, "send the DCS 0x51 brightness write in HS mode (default: LP)");
+
 static int ams678_er2_plus_dsc_on(struct ams678_er2_plus_dsc *ctx)
 {
 	struct mipi_dsi_multi_context dsi_ctx = { .dsi = ctx->dsi };
@@ -410,22 +419,31 @@
 	}
 	mode_flags = dsi->mode_flags;
 	/*
-	 * The panel ignores 0x51 sent in HS mode: the DBV stays at the value
-	 * last written in LP mode (0 from enable), so the screen stays dark.
+	 * Before the msm command DMA FIFO watermark fix (dma_fifo_ctrl) a DCS
+	 * write in HS mode never reached the panel and an LP long write lost
+	 * its last payload byte, which left only DBV[9:8] (four levels). With
+	 * the DMA burst intact the full 10-bit DBV arrives; keep LP as the
+	 * default transfer mode (known good) and let bl_hs select stock's HS.
 	 */
-	dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
+	if (bl_hs)
+		dsi->mode_flags &= ~MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
+	else
+		dsi->mode_flags |= MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM;
 
 	/*
-	 * Only the first 0x51 byte reaches the panel through the Iris6 analog
-	 * bypass: it sets DBV[9:8], giving off plus three visible levels (a lone
-	 * byte, the second byte or a generic long write change nothing else).
-	 * Spread 1..1023 over those three levels so only 0 is dark; the plain
-	 * high byte made every value below 256 black.
+	 * Stock (dsi_anakin_backlightupdate) never sends DBV 1 or 9 to this
+	 * panel; keep its substitutions.
 	 */
-	if (brightness)
-		brightness = (1 + (brightness - 1) * 3 / 1023) << 8;
+	if (brightness == 1)
+		brightness = 2;
+	else if (brightness == 9)
+		brightness = 10;
 
-	/* Vendor inverted-DBV handling sends the high byte first. */
+	/*
+	 * Vendor inverted-DBV handling: the packet on the wire is the DCS long
+	 * write 0x51 with the two payload bytes {DBV[15:8], DBV[7:0]} (the
+	 * same shape stock sends: "39 01 00 00 00 00 03 51 hh ll").
+	 */
 	ret = mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(dsi, brightness);
 	dsi->mode_flags = mode_flags;
 
